# Tashil Aqar Linear ticket workflow

Follow this on every task. Canonical process: https://linear.app/sw-point/document/nzam-altyktat-walmrahl-tashil-aqar-28a1cf0574c8

- **Workspace:** `sw-point`
- **Team:** Tashil Aqar
- **Issue key:** `TAQ`
- **Project:** Website — tashilaqar.com

## No ticket, no work

Every idea, proposal, feature, and fix gets a numbered `TAQ` issue before any code, branch, or PR. If none is given, ask for one or flag that it is missing. Do not start silently.

## Labels

Each ticket carries:

- **Type** — exactly one: New Feature, Enhancement, Bug Report, Test Finding, UI/UX, Content/Copy, Security, Performance, Tech Debt, Research, Legal/Compliance.
- **Stage** — exactly one. Change it at every transition (list below).
- **Area** — one or more: Web, Mobile iOS, Mobile Android, Backend/Functions, Firestore/Rules, Hosting/Infra, Design System (M3), Localization/RTL.
- **Source** — exactly one (test findings use the real source, e.g. User Test).
- **Severity** — required on Bug Report and Test Finding. An open **Critical** or **High** blocks production.

## Status and stage

Move status and the Stage label together. Do not skip gates.

| Status | Stage label |
| --- | --- |
| Triage, Backlog | Idea |
| Proposal, Todo | Proposed |
| Approved | Approved |
| In Progress | Building |
| In Review (PR) | PR Open |
| On Dev | On Dev |
| Testing | Testing |
| Fix Needed | Test Failed |
| Ready for Prod | Fixed |
| Done (on prod) | On Prod |

`Canceled` and `Duplicate` close the ticket with no further stage. `Fix Needed` is the testing-failure branch, not a step on the happy path.

## Test findings

Each problem found in testing is a **sub-issue** of the original ticket:

- Title: `[Test] …`
- Labels: Type = Test Finding, plus Severity and Source (e.g. User Test).
- Move the parent to **Fix Needed** / Stage **Test Failed**.
- Close the sub-issue only after the fix is retested on the **new SHA**.
- Move the parent to **Ready for Prod** only when every sub-issue is closed and the parent passes retest.
- An open Critical or High blocks production.

## Naming and linking

- Branch names include `taq-<n>` (example: `taq-12-short-name`).
- PR titles start with `[TAQ-<n>]`.
- Commit messages start with `TAQ-<n>:`.
- Link the PR to the Linear issue (issue URL in the PR body). Do not use `Fixes` / `Closes` / `Resolves`; a merge must not mark the issue Done before On Dev, testing, and Mohamed's production OK.

## Release

- Land changes on `dev` first. The User Test agent tests that **exact dev SHA** — record the SHA on the ticket.
- Do not merge to `main` or `master`, and do not deploy, without Mohamed's explicit OK.
- This repo is public. Never commit secrets, tokens, or credentials.
- Do not delete demo or test accounts.
